descriptionByLocale.en:
Your mission You participate in the management of questions and testimonies of the public for interactive live broadcasts, you carry out various searches for information with specialists, mainly by phone, online and also in the field. You will be looking for specialists, witnesses and useful addresses related to the themes to be covered in the show. You also compile investigation files for the production of programmes and prepare summaries for journalists and finally, you propose programme topics in the field of services and consumption. Your profile
• Very good general knowledge and curiosity;
• Strong interest in investigation, investigation and radio material;
• Interest in the field of services and consumption;
• Good knowledge of Swiss institutions;
• Good knowledge of social networks and internet research;
• Proficiency in office applications (e.g. Teams, MS Office);
• Knowledge of German and English (read and spoken). What we offer
• A motivating work environment in a captivating environment.
• Immersion in a motivated and cohesive team.
• The opportunity to discover a public service audiovisual media. The RTS offers an introductory internship in the research profession to people in training, within the radio program "On en

